SELECT gen_random_uuid(), 'Front Plate Raise', 'Front Plate Raise is an exercise targeting Shoulders.', 'The plate front raise is a variation of the dumbbell front raise where the lifter holds a weight plate between two hands, rather than using a dumbbell, barbell, or other weight. It can provide variety in a shoulder-focused muscle-building workout, or as part of an upper body or full-body circuit. 1. While standing straight, hold a barbell plate in both hands at the 3 and 9 o''clock positions. Your palms should be facing each other and your arms should be extended and locked with a slight bend at the elbows and the plate should be down near your waist in front of you as far as you can go. **Tip**: The arms will remain in this position throughout the exercise. This will be your starting position. 2. Slowly raise the plate as you exhale until it is a little above shoulder level. Hold the contraction for a second. As you inhale, slowly lower the plate back down to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', 'GYM', 'Shoulders', 'Shoulders', 'BEGINNER', 5, NULL, NULL, 0, '[]', NULL, 'Keep the movement controlled, avoid momentum, and stop if pain occurs.', true, 3, 10, NULL, 'Shoulders', 60, NULL, NULL, 'strength', NULL
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM exercises WHERE lower(name) = lower('Front Plate Raise') AND exercise_type = 'GYM');

